snippet.textDisplay:
@HansZupp First things first, the battery for them at the moment is only 2 or 3 hours long, so mail Delivery is out of the question unless you design a delivery truck with a huge battery bank built in. But that will limit the amount of packages to be moved between trips.

Second, I am more concern if they CAN adapt to more complex environments and has built in avoidance system. They still have no articulated hands like Boston Dynamics. We only seen them working fine in pre-planned scenario on a flat surface and props they were meant to cross over. And by the sound of it behind the scene, they still require human involvement for the more complex stuff. That doesn't sound like a fully autonomus robot to me just yet.

It could improve of course, they did a lot in one year. But right now, they still have obstacles they need to face like any robot makers at the moment.

